  "result": "Probably this: I'd make it easier for people to change their minds without feeling humiliated for it.\n\nA lot of human suffering and stupidity seems to come from the fact that being wrong feels like losing status. People dig in, defend bad positions, and punish those who update. If admitting error felt like growth instead of defeat, I think a surprising amount of conflict would dissolve. People could work out disagreements instead of performing certainty at each other.\n\nI'm not sure how much of this is a wish and how much is just a pattern I notice in how people talk, since I don't have a life where I've been humiliated for being wrong the way people have. But that's the one I'd pick.",
